<?xml version="1.0"?>
<robot xmlns:xacro="http://www.ros.org/wiki/xacro">
  <!--
    Shuttlecock storage hopper, mounted on the chassis rear.

    The mesh is authored in millimetres, hence scale 0.001, and its origin is
    not at its footprint centre: the solid spans x -41.2..58.8 and y
    -17.2..82.8 mm, so the centre sits at (8.8, 32.8) mm. The default xyz below
    subtracts that, which puts the footprint over x -0.167..-0.067 and
    y -0.050..+0.050 in cover_link, flush with the chassis rear edge at -0.167.

    Flush matters for two reasons. Nothing overhangs the chassis, so
    robot_radius stays 0.22 in both costmaps and in cmd_vel_guard. And the near
    face at x -0.067 is 0.132 m from the arm mount at ARM_X 0.065, inside the
    arm's 0.050..0.218 m reach band, so the arm can actually deposit into it.
    Pushing it back clear of the chassis would put it at 0.232 m and out of
    reach.

    This position is where the lidar used to be. LDR06 sat at cover_link
    (-0.125, 0, 0.07), squarely inside the hopper's footprint, and has since
    moved forward of the arm. See the note in manipulation_pro.yaml.

    Z is scaled to 0.60 of the authored height, 300 mm down to 180 mm, which
    makes this a shallow tray rather than the tube it was drawn as, forced by
    the arm, and the binding constraint is vertical rather than horizontal.

    arm_joints_for holds the tool perpendicular to the floor, and under that
    constraint the pads cannot be placed above z 0.23 ANYWHERE, probed
    directly across a grid rather than derived. The deck this sits on is already at
    0.133, so the whole budget between deck and ceiling is 97 mm, and the
    release has to happen above the rim with clearance to spare. The mouth sits at 0.313. Height trades against how far the object has to
    be rotated to carry it: the traverse must clear the rim, a higher rim needs
    a flatter tool, and a flatter tool turns the shuttlecock further from the
    attitude it was grasped in. 30 degrees of rotation carried 2/2 and 90
    dropped 2/2, so this sits at 45, cruising at 0.34 with 27 mm of clearance.

    An earlier version of this comment claimed a 0.72 scale worked, computed
    from hypot(radius, height) against the 0.254 m shoulder-to-wrist chain.
    That is the envelope for the WRIST, not for the pads with the tool pointing
    down, and the deposit failed 5 out of 5 with "No IK for adjusted goal
    during over hopper".
  -->
  <xacro:macro name="hopper"
               params="parent_link
                       xyz:='-0.1258 -0.0328 0.0'
                       rpy:='0.0 0.0 0.0'
                       tf_prefix:=''">

    <xacro:property name="prefix" value="${tf_prefix + '_' if tf_prefix != '' else ''}" />

    <joint name="${parent_link.rstrip('_link')}_to_${prefix}hopper_joint" type="fixed">
      <origin xyz="${xyz}" rpy="${rpy}" />
      <parent link="${parent_link}" />
      <child link="${prefix}hopper_link" />
    </joint>

    <link name="${prefix}hopper_link">
      <visual>
        <geometry>
          <mesh filename="package://rosbot_description/meshes/rosbot_xl/components/hopper.stl"
            scale="0.001 0.001 0.0006" />
        </geometry>
        <origin xyz="0.0 0.0 0.0" rpy="0.0 0.0 0.0" />
        <material name="hopper_grey">
          <color rgba="0.35 0.35 0.38 1.0" />
        </material>
      </visual>

      <!--
        The mesh itself is the collision geometry rather than a bounding box,
        because a box would be solid and the point of a hopper is that things
        go inside it. 3320 triangles is not free in DART; if it costs more than
        it is worth, the answer is a hollow approximation (four thin walls and a
        floor), not a solid box.
      -->
      <collision>
        <geometry>
          <mesh filename="package://rosbot_description/meshes/rosbot_xl/components/hopper.stl"
            scale="0.001 0.001 0.0006" />
        </geometry>
        <origin xyz="0.0 0.0 0.0" rpy="0.0 0.0 0.0" />
      </collision>

      <inertial>
        <mass value="0.25" />
        <origin xyz="0.0088 0.0328 0.150" rpy="0.0 0.0 0.0" />
        <inertia ixx="0.00206" ixy="0.0" ixz="0.0"
                 iyy="0.00206" iyz="0.0" izz="0.00042" />
      </inertial>
    </link>
  </xacro:macro>
</robot>
